00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:36.102
PARNA BHATTACHARYA: Yeah.

00:31:38.420 --> 00:31:41.280
All right, the next one--
could the Apigee API be used

00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:42.570
for monitoring service--

00:31:42.570 --> 00:31:46.840
service management, incident
management escalations?

00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:50.750
So Apigee acts as
a abstraction layer

00:31:50.750 --> 00:31:53.600
of facade, which
means that Apigee

00:31:53.600 --> 00:32:00.320
can be leveraged for monitoring
your APIs, SLAs and SLOs.

00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:03.290
And, in fact, that's
something which

00:32:03.290 --> 00:32:05.930
Woolworths uses significantly.

00:32:05.930 --> 00:32:09.480
Josh, you want to share your
experience with API Monitoring?

00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:12.020
JOSHUA ROGERS: Yeah, so we
utilize API Monitoring to make

00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:14.450
sure that our back end
services understand

00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:18.650
what scale of traffic is
coming through the platform.

00:32:18.650 --> 00:32:22.320
When we're caching on the front
end or within the Apigee layer,

00:32:22.320 --> 00:32:25.370
it's not always
clear, a small change

00:32:25.370 --> 00:32:28.400
that introduces
entropy or a dynamicity

00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:30.620
into the requests,
how much of an effect

00:32:30.620 --> 00:32:34.350
that might have if it's not
able to cache it on that layer.

00:32:34.350 --> 00:32:37.010
So we want to make sure that
we're very cognizant of how

00:32:37.010 --> 00:32:38.960
much traffic is
flowing through Apigee,

00:32:38.960 --> 00:32:41.682
and we utilize our learning
and different dynamics--

00:32:41.682 --> 00:32:43.640
there's multiple different
dimensions available

00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:44.720
to measure--

00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:49.940
to alert us of any changes
in the transactions as well.

00:32:49.940 --> 00:32:52.930
PARNA BHATTACHARYA: Absolutely.

00:32:52.930 --> 00:32:54.070
Question from Allstate.

00:32:54.070 --> 00:32:56.950
